{"run": "digest", "t": 32656, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Armed conflicts and attacks] 2026 Iran war — The United Arab Emirates defence ministry reports that an Iranian drone has been intercepted over the country's airspace. Additionally, Iran's army also says that they have attacked the Al Minhad Air Base, which the UAE also denies."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 32656, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Armed conflicts and attacks] Gaza war — Israeli attacks across the Gaza Strip kill ⁠at least five people."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 32656, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Arts and culture] Death of Dolly Parton — The estate of former American country singer Dolly Parton announces that two DollyFest festivals will be held next year in London, United Kingdom, and Nashville, Tennessee, U.S., to honor her life and legacy."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 32656, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Disasters and accidents] 2026 Nepal floods — It is reported that school principal Rajendra Dawadi has saved over 900 students and 16 faculty members at the Tribhuvan Trishuli Secondary School in Bidur, Nuwakot District, Nepal, 10 minutes before flash floods hit the area last week."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 32656, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Disasters and accidents] 2026 Nepal floods — The death toll from the flash floods in Nepal has reached past 950. Additionally, hundreds are reported to be feared stuck in hydropower tunnels in wake of the floods."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 32656, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Disasters and accidents] The Mount Sinabung stratovolcano in North Sumatra, Indonesia, erupts, sending 3,500 meters of ash in the air. No casualties are reported."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 32656, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Health and environment] 2026 Ebola epidemic — The total amount of cases of ebola in the Democratic Republic of the Congo exceeds 6,000."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 32656, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Health and environment] A data from the Methane Alert and Response System reports that Turkmenistan has started the process of clearing methane leaks from its oil and gas facilities."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 32656, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [International relations] Greece–Israel relations, 2020s European rearmament — Israel and Greece sign a {{Euro}}3 billion (US$3.48 billion) arms export deal that will enable the Israeli defense ministry to build the \"Achilles Shield\", a multi-layered air defense array similar to the Iron Dome, made entirely by Israeli"}
{"run": "digest", "t": 32657, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [International relations] Italy–Spain relations — Italian prime minister Giorgia Meloni announces the Italian government will extend its suspension of the Schengen free movement agreement with Spain for another 15 days in response to the brief migrant crisis event at the Ceuta border fence"}
{"run": "digest", "t": 32657, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Law and crime] Corruption in South Korea, Unification Church and politics — A South Korean court sentences Unification Church leader Hak Ja Han to two years in prison for bribing officials, including former first lady Kim Keon Hee, in an effort to obtain policy favors."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 32657, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Law and crime] Kidnapping of Shelly Kittleson — A judiciary in Iraq sentences Kata'ib Hezbollah member Amir Rahim Jabbar to 15 years in prison for his role in the kidnapping of American journalist Shelly Kittleson."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 32657, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Law and crime] Swiss police arrest a suspect for the mass shooting at a rave in Aarau, Aargau, over the weekend, which killed an Italian woman and injured several other people."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 32657, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Politics and elections] 2025–2026 Kosovo political deadlock — Kosovo's Vetëvendosje and Democratic League parties agree to support former Constitutional Court judge Bekim Sejdiu for president, potentially ending nearly two years of political deadlock and enabling the formation of a new government."}
